2.31.m:
Sanatkumāra said:
Now [I will describe] another subtle mountain, of little material yet of great fruit;
at a time when materials are merely minimal, a middling [procedure] is prescribed.

One should also make the lords of obstacles with the previously stated measure of gold;
having worshipped them according to rule with perfumes, flowers, and the like, in order—

Thus ends the thirty-first chapter in the Uttarabhāga of the glorious Liṅga Mahāpurāṇa.

2.32.m:
Sanatkumāra said:
The recitation, fire oblation, worship, giving, consecration, and other rites are as before;
I shall describe in brief the gift of the golden earth.

And one should worship Śaṅkara, Śiva, with a thousand jars and the like;
the excellent gift of the golden earth has been proclaimed in this Purāṇa of the Liṅga.

Thus ends the thirty-second chapter, entitled "The Gift of the Golden Earth", in the Uttarabhāga of the glorious Liṅga Mahāpurāṇa.

2.33.m:
Sanatkumāra said:
Now I shall proclaim another excellent [gift], the wish-granting tree;
having made it with a hundred niṣkas, endowed with all its branches,

2.34.m:
Sanatkumāra said:
I shall proclaim the gift of Gaṇeśeśa in the previously mentioned pavilion;
having worshipped the god of the gods of gods, surrounded by the world protectors,
